# UX-SPEC.md §3.13 and [D-18] · KEYMAP.md §First run — the first-run card on a Fleet that has
# never been run, and the four keys it still answers.
#
# `FirstRun` is full-window and shadows everything except `ctrl-q` (KEYMAP §Modes), so the two
# things worth pinning are that a fresh `empty` home reaches it at all — every other preset must
# never show it — and that shadowing the Hub does not cost the card its own documented keys.
# `?` is the safe one of the four: `N` and `n` open dialogs that write, and `i` is only drawn
# when `~/.swarm/state.json` exists, which a hermetic home never has.
#
# Headless: virtual-lane only, because of its `shot`. The keyboard does reach the focused view
# in the headless lane (§7), so everything else here would run there.
fixture: empty
await idle 20000
assert key_contexts[0] == "FirstRun" && key_contexts[1] absent
assert lists.worktrees.rows[0] absent && lists.prs.rows[0] absent && lists.jobs.rows[0] absent
assert daemon.link == connected && sticky_error absent
shot first-run

# The card shadows the Hub, and still answers `?`.
key ?
await overlay == Dialog 5000
assert dialog.name == "Help"

# Closing it returns to the card rather than to a Hub that has nothing in it.
key escape
await overlay absent 5000
assert key_contexts[0] == "FirstRun"
dump first-run
quit
